  "title": "A geometric shape regularity effect in the human brain: MEG dataset",
  "description": "This magnetoencephalography (MEG) dataset comprises recordings from 20 adult participants viewing simple geometric shapes (hexagons, triangles, quadrilaterals) and other visual stimuli. The study investigates the neural mechanisms underlying human perception of regular geometric shapes, examining how the brain processes discrete geometric regularities such as symmetries and parallelism. The dataset supports research into the specialized brain systems engaged in abstract geometric perception and their distinction from general visual processing.",
  "methods_description": "MEG data were collected during visual perception tasks involving geometric shapes and control stimuli. Participants viewed simple shapes including hexagons, triangles, and quadrilaterals. Data were anonymized and defaced using mne_bids (v0.16.0) with shuffled participant order, modified dates, and stripped gender information. Pre-processing was performed using mne-bids-pipeline with a custom configuration file.",
